# <How to <verb> <object>>

<Punchline: Rotate compromised or expiring staging API keys with zero service downtime in under 3 minutes.>

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Prerequisites & Permissions**:
> - Active Vault authentication session (`vault token lookup`)
> - Kubernetes cluster context set to staging (`kubectl config current-context`)

---

## When to use this recipe

- Scenario 1: Staging credentials expire or are leaked in logs.
- Scenario 2: Routine quarterly secret rotation policy.

---

## Action Steps

### Step 1 — Generate and Store New Secret in Vault

<Explain the "Why" behind parameters.>

```bash
export VAULT_ADDR="https://vault.staging.internal:8200"

# Generate 32-byte cryptographically secure token
NEW_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)

vault kv put secret/staging/auth-service/api-keys \
  primary_key="${NEW_KEY}" \
  rotation_epoch="$(date +%s)"
```

```
Success! Data written to: secret/staging/auth-service/api-keys
```

---

### Step 2 — Trigger Zero-Downtime Rolling Restart

```bash
kubectl rollout restart deployment/auth-service -n staging
kubectl rollout status deployment/auth-service -n staging --timeout=60s
```

```
deployment.apps/auth-service restarted
Waiting for deployment "auth-service" rollout to finish: 1 of 2 updated replicas are available...
deployment "auth-service" successfully rolled out
```

---

### Step 3 — Verify Secret Propagation

```bash
curl -i -H "Authorization: Bearer ${NEW_KEY}" https://auth.staging.internal/v1/healthz
```

```http
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"authenticated","key_epoch":"valid"}
```

---

## Troubleshooting & Common Gotchas

| Symptom / Error | Root Cause | Immediate Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `401 Unauthorized` | New secret has not mounted into the pod environment. | Inspect pod rollout status with `kubectl get pods -n staging` and wait 15s. |
| `vault: permission denied` | Vault token expired. | Re-authenticate via `vault login -method=oidc`. |
| `CrashLoopBackOff` | Secret value contained unescaped trailing newline. | Re-write Vault secret using `openssl rand -hex 32` without trailing `\n`. |

